1. Code and rules ported into Dualyrics
---------------------------------------

LiveTranslate
  https://github.com/TheDeathDragon/LiveTranslate
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Shiro
  Used: the speech segmentation rules of vad_processor.py (VADProcessor) and the
  interim-commit rules of main.py (_do_interim_asr, _strip_committed_overlap,
  _is_short_utterance), rewritten without numpy/torch; the idea of
  model_manager.py (_hf_repo_complete) for checking that a download is complete;
  (v2.2.1) the rules of the repetition check of translator.py (an answer of at
  least 40 characters repeating a piece of 8 or more) and of the noise filter of
  _process_segment (a piece of 2 s or more with 3 alphanumerics or fewer).
  In: dualyrics/live/vad.py, dualyrics/live/interim.py, dualyrics/live/engine.py,
  dualyrics/live/models.py, dualyrics/dub/piper.py, dualyrics/live/deps.py,
  dualyrics/translate.py (is_looping), dualyrics/live/text.py

Silero VAD
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team
  Used: the streaming call of the ONNX model (512-sample windows at 16 kHz,
  64 samples of context, recurrent state carried over). The model file itself
  is not bundled; it is loaded from the faster-whisper package when installed.
  In: dualyrics/live/silero.py

faster-whisper
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 SYSTRAN
  Used: the location of the bundled Silero model (faster_whisper/assets), its
  h/c inputs and the ONNX Runtime session options of faster_whisper/vad.py.
  faster-whisper is also the optional speech recogniser of Live mode
  (downloaded by the user, not bundled).
  In: dualyrics/live/silero.py

LiveCaptions-Translator
  https://github.com/SakiRinn/LiveCaptions-Translator
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2024 SakiRinn and other contributors
  Used (behaviour re-implemented in Python, no source text copied):
  src/utils/LiveCaptionsHandler.cs (starting and hiding Live Captions, the
  LiveCaptionsDesktopWindow / CaptionsTextBlock lookup, recovery), the sync loop
  of src/Translator.cs (25 ms polling, sentence end, idle and change counters)
  and src/models/TranslationTaskQueue.cs (dropping stale translations).
  Changed: a Live Captions window the user opened is left alone, window style
  and position are restored on close, one caption is updated in place, and
  Live mode falls back to Whisper by itself.
  (v2.2.1, behaviour re-implemented) the 10-byte minimum before a change of an
  unfinished sentence counts (SHORT_THRESHOLD), newlines of CJK captions turned
  into sentence ends (TextUtil ReplaceNewlines) and long captions shortened from
  the start, preferably at a clause mark (ShortenDisplaySentence).
  In: dualyrics/live/wincaptions.py, dualyrics/live/engine.py, dualyrics/render.py

LiveCaptions-Translator-Buddy
  https://github.com/MuuCake/LiveCaptions-Translator-Buddy
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 kidoyuyu
  Used: confirmation that the Live Captions text can be read from Python with
  comtypes UI Automation (no code copied).
  In: dualyrics/live/wincaptions.py

Translumo
  https://github.com/ramjke/Translumo
  Apache License 2.0 (the upstream LICENSE names no copyright holder;
  copyright of the Translumo authors)
  Used: ported to Python from
  src/Translumo.Processing/TextProcessing/TextResultCacheService.cs and
  src/Translumo.Utils/Extensions/StringExtensions.cs: Jaro and Sorensen-Dice
  similarity, the near-duplicate cache rules and their constants.
  Changed: OCR readings score by their number of letters, UI Automation
  readings count as trusted, and a repeated line reuses its earlier
  translation (see the header of dualyrics/screen/dedupe.py).
  In: dualyrics/screen/dedupe.py, dualyrics/screen/engine.py,
  dualyrics/live/engine.py

Argos Translate
  https://github.com/argosopentech/argos-translate
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Argos Open Technologies, LLC
  Used: the .argosmodel package layout and metadata fields
  (argostranslate/package.py), the argospm-index format, and the CTranslate2 /
  SentencePiece translation call (argostranslate/translate.py,
  argostranslate/tokenizer.py), rewritten without the argostranslate package.
  The language models are downloaded by the user and keep their own licences.
  In: dualyrics/offline.py, dualyrics/ui/keys_page.py

dota-live-translator
  https://github.com/fr0styJS/dota-live-translator
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Fr0styDev
  Used: ported from backend/procloop.py: the ctypes/comtypes declarations and
  the call sequence of WASAPI process loopback capture
  (ActivateAudioInterfaceAsync, IAudioClient, IAudioCaptureClient).
  Changed: exclude mode for Dualyrics' own process, 16 kHz mono with a 48 kHz
  fallback, a stateful resampler, process-exit check, one error type for the
  fallback to system loopback.
  In: dualyrics/live/procloop.py, dualyrics/live/capture.py

OverTranslate
  https://github.com/Hon-Lu/OverTranslate
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Hon-Lu
  Used (v2.2.1, rules re-implemented, no source text copied): the retry
  schedule of Services/Realtime/RealtimeRetryBackoff (1 s, 2 s, then 4 s, a few
  attempts while the line is still shown, reset on success).
  In: dualyrics/retry.py, dualyrics/screen/engine.py, dualyrics/live/engine.py

Mimi
  https://github.com/yuxino/Mimi
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 yuxino
  Used (v2.2.1, rules re-implemented, no source text copied): the translation
  policy of shared/mimi-core/src/translation_policy.rs: a deadline of about
  5 s for one live line before the next provider, and a longer back-off
  (4 s, then 8 s) after a rate limit.
  In: dualyrics/translate.py, dualyrics/live/livetranslate.py, dualyrics/retry.py

Windows classic samples (ApplicationLoopback)
  https://github.com/microsoft/Windows-classic-samples
  MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
  Used: the documented activation sequence of Samples/ApplicationLoopback,
  which the port above follows (no code copied directly).
  In: dualyrics/live/procloop.py


